{
 "shelf": "errors",
 "origin": "overlay",
 "about": "What is written by hand about the compiler's diagnostics: which ones come together, the concept behind each, a right example, and who reads it (the errors of dialect files are for dialect authors, not for the local agents).",
 "rows": [
  {"id": "error:N0002", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0005"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0004"}], "tags": ["indentation"]},
  {"id": "error:N0004", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0005"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0002"}], "tags": ["indentation"],
   "add": ["**Seen with.** A block closed with `}` or a line pasted from another language: fix `N0022` on the lines above first; the indentation errors usually go with it."]},
  {"id": "error:N0005", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0002"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0004"}], "tags": ["indentation"]},
  {"id": "error:N0006", "links": [{"rel": "often-is", "to": "error:N0022"}, {"rel": "often-is", "to": "error:N0009"}], "tags": ["syntax"],
   "add": ["**Seen with.** `#` is a comment of another language (`//` in Nuclear); `&` alone is not an operator."]},
  {"id": "error:N0007", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0010"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0011"}], "tags": ["strings"]},
  {"id": "error:N0008", "links": [{"rel": "often-with", "to": "error:N0013"}], "tags": ["syntax"]},
  {"id": "error:N0009", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0022"}, {"rel": "habit", "to": "habit:and-or-not-x"}], "tags": ["habit"],
   "add": ["**Right.** `and`, `or`, `not x`, `==`, `!=`, and no `;` at the end of a line."]},
  {"id": "error:N0010", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0007"}], "tags": ["strings"]},
  {"id": "error:N0011", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0007"}], "tags": ["strings"],
   "add": ["**Tip.** A regular expression is a raw string: `r\"\\d+\"` needs no escapes."]},
  {"id": "error:N0001", "links": [{"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0019"}], "tags": ["names"]},
  {"id": "error:N0013", "links": [{"rel": "often-is", "to": "pitfall:decorator-after-its-field"}, {"rel": "often-with", "to": "error:N0008"}, {"rel": "often-is", "to": "error:N0022"}], "tags": ["syntax", "decorators"],
   "add": [
    "**Most common cause.** A decorator written after the field or method it belongs to, or on the same line: the message is `'@column' has no member below it`. A decorator goes on the line right above its member:",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "@entity(\"readers\")",
    "entity Reader()",
    "  @primary(generated = true)",
    "  id: int",
    "  @column(length = 80, unique = true)",
    "  email: string",
    "```"
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0016", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0017"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0018"}], "tags": ["modules"]},
  {"id": "error:N0017", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0016"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0018"}], "tags": ["modules"],
   "add": ["**Right.** Inside a module (a class, a kind) only fields and methods: `count: int = 0` is a field; an assignment belongs inside a method."]},
  {"id": "error:N0018", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0017"}], "tags": ["modules"]},
  {"id": "error:N0019", "links": [{"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0102"}, {"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0001"}], "tags": ["names"],
   "add": ["**Seen with.** A local variable named like a method of its own module (`pieces = ~pieces(raw)`): give the variable another name (`planned = ~pieces(raw)`)."]},
  {"id": "error:N0020", "links": [{"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0016"}], "tags": ["functions"]},
  {"id": "error:N0021", "tags": ["comments"]},
  {"id": "error:N0022", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0009"}, {"rel": "hides", "to": "error:N0013"}, {"rel": "hides", "to": "error:N0004"}, {"rel": "concept", "to": "faq:learn-the-syntax"}, {"rel": "playbook", "to": "playbook:fix-compiler-errors"}], "tags": ["habit"],
   "asks": ["why is await an error", "why can't I use const", "why are braces an error"],
   "add": [
    "**Fix it first.** The compiler hides the other errors of a line that has a habit, because they only repeat the same mistake. `nuclear fix` applies the exact ones.",
    "",
    "**The whole of it, right:**",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "// no braces, no semicolons, no const, no new, no await, no return on the last line",
    "greet(user: User, times: int = 1) string",
    "  name = user.name.trim()",
    "  if times > 1",
    "    return \"Hi ${name}, again\"",
    "  \"Hi ${name}\"",
    "```",
    "",
    "Each habit has its row: `habit:` (search the word you wrote: `await`, `const`, `new`, `import`, `class`, `switch`)."
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0102", "links": [{"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0019"}, {"rel": "in-a-project", "to": "error:N0303"}], "tags": ["names"],
   "add": ["**Seen with.** A small model that writes the same method twice, or copies into its file a declaration another file already has: write only what the task declares."]},
  {"id": "error:N0103", "tags": ["expressions"],
   "add": ["**Right.** Give the branch a variable first: `label = if a` + its branches, then `f(label)`."]},
  {"id": "error:N0105", "links": [{"rel": "then", "to": "error:N0106"}], "tags": ["names", "scope"],
   "add": ["**Right.** Create the variable before the block and assign it inside, or make the `if` the value: `text = if ok` + branches."]},
  {"id": "error:N0106", "links": [{"rel": "often-after", "to": "error:N0105"}, {"rel": "a-class-is", "to": "error:N0220"}, {"rel": "a-member-is", "to": "error:N0116"}, {"rel": "library-is", "to": "error:N0114"}], "tags": ["names"],
   "add": ["**Check, in this order.** A typo; a variable created inside an `if` or `for` and read after it (`N0105`); a parameter the method does not have; a name of the target's library the dialect does not know (`nuclear defs search <text>`); a declaration of another file that the task forgot to list."]},
  {"id": "error:N0107", "tags": ["patterns"]},
  {"id": "error:N0108", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:result"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0109"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0110"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0111"}, {"rel": "kind-rule", "to": "error:N0216"}], "tags": ["result"],
   "add": ["**Right.** Either make the function return a `Result` (then `user = findUser(id)` unwraps it and an `Err` leaves by itself), or handle both cases: `match findUser(id)` + `Ok(user) -> ...` / `Err(e) -> ...`."]},
  {"id": "error:N0109", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:result"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0108"}], "tags": ["result"]},
  {"id": "error:N0110", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:result"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0108"}], "tags": ["result"]},
  {"id": "error:N0111", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:result"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0108"}, {"rel": "often-is", "to": "error:N0222"}], "tags": ["result"]},
  {"id": "error:N0112", "links": [{"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0221"}, {"rel": "kind", "to": "kind:backend.appcomponent"}], "tags": ["alias"]},
  {"id": "error:N0113", "tags": ["structure"]},
  {"id": "error:N0114", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:standard-library"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0115"}, {"rel": "a-project-member-is", "to": "error:N0116"}, {"rel": "members", "to": "lib:string"}, {"rel": "members", "to": "lib:list"}, {"rel": "members", "to": "lib:map"}, {"rel": "functions", "to": "lib:functions"}, {"rel": "result-read-is", "to": "error:N0222"}, {"rel": "pitfall", "to": "pitfall:library-names-of-other-languages"}], "tags": ["library"],
   "asks": ["why is push not allowed", "how do I get the length of a list", "why is contains an error"],
   "add": [
    "**Right.**",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "tidy(names: string[], text: string) string",
    "  names.add(text.upper())",
    "  if \"Ana\" in names",
    "    return \"found among ${names.length}\"",
    "  text.trim()",
    "```",
    "",
    "`add` not `push` or `append`; `upper()` not `toUpperCase()`; `length` is a property (no parentheses) and never `len(x)`; membership is `x in xs`, never `contains` or `includes`.",
    "",
    "**In a test.** `found.length` on a kept `Result` is this error too: read `found.value.length`."
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0115", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:standard-library"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0114"}, {"rel": "limit", "to": "limit:untyped-values"}], "tags": ["library", "types"]},
  {"id": "error:N0116", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0114"}, {"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0106"}, {"rel": "contract", "to": "concept:contracts"}], "tags": ["names", "members"],
   "add": ["**Check.** The message lists every member the declaration has: use one of them. A repository's own methods are `find`, `findAll`, `save`, `remove`; a model of a contract changed when the backend changed (build the backend, or `nuclear contracts update`)."]},
  {"id": "error:N0201", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:kinds"}, {"rel": "plugin-kind-is", "to": "error:N0304"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0209"}], "tags": ["kinds"],
   "add": ["**Check.** The word before the name must be a kind of the project's platform (`nuclear help words --platform <p>`): `usecase`, not `use case`; `appcomponent`, not `component` on the backend; a kind of the mobile platform does not exist on the backend."]},
  {"id": "error:N0202", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0203", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0204", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0205", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0206", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0207", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0208", "tags": ["inheritance"]},
  {"id": "error:N0209", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0215"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0216"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0221"}], "tags": ["kinds"]},
  {"id": "error:N0210", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0211", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0212", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0213", "agents": false, "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0214"}]},
  {"id": "error:N0214", "agents": false, "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0213"}]},
  {"id": "error:N0215", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0216"}, {"rel": "kind", "to": "kind:backend.usecase"}, {"rel": "playbook", "to": "playbook:add-a-use-case"}], "tags": ["kinds", "usecase"], "meta": {"kinds": ["usecase"]},
   "add": ["**Right.** One use case, one operation: a second operation is a second `usecase` file. A helper several use cases share is a `service`."]},
  {"id": "error:N0216", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0215"}, {"rel": "kind", "to": "kind:backend.usecase"}, {"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:result"}], "tags": ["kinds", "usecase", "result"], "meta": {"kinds": ["usecase"]},
   "add": [
    "**Right.**",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "usecase BooksOfAuthor(books: BookRepository)",
    "  exec(author: string) Result<Error, Book[]>",
    "    Ok(~books.byAuthor(author))",
    "```"
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0217", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0309"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0308"}], "tags": ["decorators"],
   "add": ["**Check.** The message lists the arguments the decorator has. Look it up: `nuclear help <decorator> --platform <p>`."]},
  {"id": "error:N0218", "tags": ["kinds", "generics"], "meta": {"kinds": ["statemanager"]}},
  {"id": "error:N0219", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:type-definitions"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0220"}], "tags": ["type-definitions"]},
  {"id": "error:N0220", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:type-definitions"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0219"}, {"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0106"}, {"rel": "in-a-run", "to": "failure:a-test-names-a-class-nobody-planned"}], "tags": ["names", "type-definitions"],
   "add": ["**Check.** A typo in a class of a library (the message gives the closest one); or a class of the project that no file declares: `inject<BooksAppComponent>()` needs a file that declares `appcomponent BooksAppComponent`. In a run of the Loop this means the plan missed a piece."]},
  {"id": "error:N0221", "links": [{"rel": "kind", "to": "kind:backend.appcomponent"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0112"}, {"rel": "pitfall", "to": "pitfall:appcomponent-only-aliases"}], "tags": ["kinds", "appcomponent"], "meta": {"kinds": ["appcomponent"]},
   "add": [
    "**Right.** An application component is only aliases to use cases:",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "appcomponent BooksAppComponent",
    "  booksOf() = BooksOfAuthor.exec",
    "  create() = CreateBook.exec",
    "```"
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0222", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:result"}, {"rel": "often-with", "to": "error:N0114"}, {"rel": "often-with", "to": "error:N0111"}, {"rel": "pitfall", "to": "pitfall:a-call-without-its-await"}], "tags": ["async"],
   "asks": ["how do I await a call", "why is my result empty"],
   "add": [
    "**Right.** Await once, keep the value, then use it:",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "usecase CountBooks(books: BookRepository)",
    "  exec(author: string) Result<Error, int>",
    "    found = ~books.byAuthor(author)",
    "    Ok(found.length)",
    "```",
    "",
    "Every call to a repository, a use case, an `appcomponent` alias, an agent or a model is asynchronous. `nuclear fix` adds the `~`."
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0301", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:project-architecture"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0302"}, {"rel": "theory", "to": "concept:clean-architecture"}], "tags": ["architecture"],
   "asks": ["why can't my controller call a repository", "who can call a use case"],
   "add": [
    "**The allowed calls.** Backend: controller → `appcomponent` → use case → repository, service or aggregate. Mobile and web: screen → state manager → `appcomponent` → use case → repository or service. Only views use the build context and navigate.",
    "",
    "**Right.**",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "@controller(\"books\")",
    "controller BooksController(books: BooksAppComponent)",
    "  @get(\"author/{author}\")",
    "  byAuthor(author: string) Result<Error, Book[]>",
    "    ~books.booksOf(author)",
    "```",
    "",
    "It is not a typo: move the call to the kind that may make it, and add the alias to the facade."
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0302", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:project-architecture"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0301"}], "tags": ["architecture"],
   "add": ["**Right.** Depend on the other component's `appcomponent` (`characters: CharactersAppComponent`), and add there the alias you need."]},
  {"id": "error:N0303", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:config"}, {"rel": "a-duplicate-is", "to": "error:N0102"}, {"rel": "failure", "to": "failure:not-inside-a-project"}], "tags": ["project"]},
  {"id": "error:N0304", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:plugins"}, {"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0201"}], "tags": ["project", "plugins"],
   "asks": ["why is agent not a kind", "how do I enable sqlite"],
   "add": [
    "**Right.** The message says the line. In `config.nuc`:",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "dragonfly(platform = \"backend\", dialect = \"fastapi\")",
    "app(name = \"books_api\")",
    "plugins(sqlite = true, ai = true, ollama = true)",
    "```"
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0305", "agents": false},
  {"id": "error:N0306", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:kinds"}, {"rel": "see-also", "to": "error:N0304"}], "tags": ["project", "kinds"]},
  {"id": "error:N0307", "links": [{"rel": "concept", "to": "concept:contracts"}, {"rel": "then", "to": "error:N0116"}], "tags": ["project", "contracts"]},
  {"id": "error:N0308", "links": [{"rel": "kind", "to": "kind:backend.entity"}, {"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0217"}], "tags": ["decorators", "relations"], "meta": {"kinds": ["entity"]},
   "add": [
    "**Right.** A relation field is optional, its type is an entity, and a `@manyToOne` keeps its column in a field of its own:",
    "",
    "```nuclear",
    "@entity(\"projects\")",
    "entity Project()",
    "  @primary(generated = true)",
    "  id: int",
    "  name: string",
    "  @oneToMany(inverse = \"project\")",
    "  tasks?: Task[]",
    "",
    "@entity(\"tasks\")",
    "entity Task()",
    "  @primary(generated = true)",
    "  id: int",
    "  title: string",
    "  projectId: int",
    "  @manyToOne(inverse = \"tasks\")",
    "  project?: Project",
    "```"
   ]},
  {"id": "error:N0309", "links": [{"rel": "same-family", "to": "error:N0217"}], "tags": ["decorators"],
   "add": ["**Check.** The decorators of a platform: `nuclear help words --platform <p>`. `@generated()` is now `@primary(generated = true)`."]}
 ]
}
